        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0786" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.796 Latin American Airways/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-09">July 9, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        17.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2500</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, I
                    have the honor to report, that Commercial Attaché Bohan has been informed by Mr.
                    Carlos Irigoyen, who is connected with the Latin American Airways, that,
                    according to cablegraphic advices, that Company is merging with another company
                    now in operation, but whose name he did not give, and that it expects to have
                    five airplanes delivered on July 12, and expects to commence operations between
                    July 20 and 25. According to the same source, the Latin American Airways has
                    been informed by the Minister of Fomento of Honduras, that he would be willing
                    to give it a contract between the city of Guatemala and Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur H.
                    Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
